A||||26||GT Bastard||Cool race against a Civic in my GT.||||14||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-18-2001||03:44 AM||||First let me say I've been ITCHING for a good race.  Around midnight or so, I decided to cruise around and enjoy the dry roads.  Played around with an ugly yellow Eclipse that gave me the ricer blow-by and I was about ready to go home.  Then comes the 96-ish 2-door Civic.  It's lowered, 17-in 5-spokes, wing, pillar guages, one of those crooked mufflers, and a DC Sports decal on both doors.  He gets right on my a$$ and my GT is getting angry.  She hates it when Hondas sniff her a$$.  Here's the cool part:  We pull away from traffic and we're side by side.  About 60ft ahead of us there's and intersection with a red light.  Beyond that, there's a really cool 3-lane bridge that goes for about a 1/4 mile or so.  The red light goes green before we get a chance to line up.  Risking a cop at the intersection, he goes full throttle.  No less than a second later, I smash the gas and chase him. The GT drops to second gear and comes to life. We fly through the intersection and he's got a couple car-lengths head start on me.  Moments later, we're going nose-to-nose.  We both glance over at each other as we approach 60mph or so(I'm wearing my evil grin.)  His Civic is SCREAMING and the GT is happily rumbling along whilst I pull ahead of him.  As we approach the end of the bridge I'm doing almost 100mph and he's about 6-7 car-legths behind me.  That was about the coolest race I've had in a looooong time.  I wanted to talk to the guy afterwords, but he didn't slow down.  <P>-Gold 87GT auto(stock except for Crane Compucam)<BR>-Gold 86SE V6, 4sp<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">    <P>"Save the planet. Go kill yourself."||||reg||14
Z||000001||TwisT||03-18-2001||04:42 AM||||Bastard,  you were on the 'loop,  weren't ya'???  =)<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000002||firstfiero||03-18-2001||11:04 AM||||    Of course he didn't slow down. Do you expect a ricer to actually act like someone with class.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Nice kill dude I had the same thing last night on my way home but it was against a honda accord. They tried to act like they didn't want to race but then hammered it off the line (Typical) but my girl reeled him in quick. Not a big deal but it was the closest thing to a street race I've seen in months.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And ya know I thought for sure that big rear spoiler and stickers would make him faster.....GO FIGURE!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
