Z||000005||Johnson's85SE||03-19-2001||03:32 PM||||HI,<BR> I know the feeling you are talking about. I one friend who just got his racing exhaust on his 1992 3.1 LTR z24. I roasted him 4 times that night. Lets just say he sold it later that month. I love racing hondas. Another friend has a souped up CRX, Headers, exhaust, intake. ect. We went at it threw three lights! I am so proud of the black beast(1985 SE V6 4SPD)Rebuilt engine, no cat. I have also beat another friends 1995 integra, with intake, dual exhaust.(The dual exhaust isn't good for performance on integra). I have lost to a 1996 Probe GT, and had a heck of a race with a 1999 civic with vtec. But I lost when the vtec kicked in, while I was in forth gear( damn highway gear). I love my 1985, but would rather have a gt body,(even though it is heavier than the SE). <BR>I will see you on the roads!      <BR><P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||14
Z||000006||fiero56||03-19-2001||06:59 PM||||I'm just twitching for a race. I've only got a few more months left on my 2.8 until it gets replaced, and my "new" injectors have restored a TON of power. I wish I could have had before and after dyno runs to compare. I did prevent a newer RAV4 from getting around me today. 'Course, I don't think those things even count. There have been several CRXs around I wouldn't mind playing with, but either they or I have always turned off.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
